d_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled payments-worker back to v3.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Finding the service:** There's no service called \"payments,\" so I first picked payments-api. A human approver turned down both the rollback and the incident for it and said the problem was in payments-worker. Nothing was changed on payments-api.\n- **Rollback:** payments-worker v3.4.0 was unhealthy in production with an 18% error rate in us-east, us-west and eu-west. v3.3.0 was its most recent release that was healthy in production, so I rolled back to that.\n- **Check:** After the rollback, payments-worker reports healthy with a 0.2% error rate.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is a SEV2 for payments-worker. It covers the bad v3.4.0 deploy and the rollback, and lists next steps: confirm recovery and find the root cause.\n\n**Still open:** payments-api is also unhealthy, with an 18% error rate on v5.1.0. Its release history marks v5.1.0 as degraded and v5.0.0 as healthy. It may just be failing because payments-worker was broken, so check whether it recovers now. If it doesn't, it may need its own rollback, which I haven't done because the approver said it was the wrong service.", "type": "text"}]}]}